# Project Rules & Constraints for PMS GLASS Portfolio

## 🛑 Strict File Length Limit
- **NEVER** write or generate any file exceeding **150 lines of code**.
- If a component or page approaches 120 lines, immediately break it down into smaller sub-components inside `src/components/ui/` or modular sub-folders.
- Separate types, mock data, animations, and custom hooks into dedicated files (`src/types/`, `src/data/`, `src/hooks/`).

## 🛠️ Architecture & Tech Stack
- **Framework:** Next.js (App Router) with TypeScript.
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS with dynamic Dark/Light themes (`next-themes`).
- **Icons:** `lucide-react`.
- **i18n:** `next-intl` supporting Arabic (`ar`, RTL, Cairo font) and English (`en`, LTR, Inter font).
- **Navigation:** Always use localized navigation hooks and components from `@/navigation` (e.g., `Link`, `useRouter`, `usePathname`), NEVER standard `next/link`.

## 🎨 Design System & Theme Rules
- **Dark Mode (Default):** Slate/Charcoal background (`#121316`), glassmorphism cards (`backdrop-blur`), and gold accents (`#F5B800`).
- **Light Mode:** Off-white background (`#F8FAFC`), crisp dark text, and subtle golden highlights.
- Always use Tailwind logical spacing classes or `dark:` modifiers for clean theme transitions.

## 📱 Multi-Page Layout Requirements
Every page must be modularized and follow standard App Router structure:
- `/` (Home)
- `/about` (About Us)
- `/services` (Services Detail)
- `/projects` (Portfolio Grid)
- `/projects/[id]` (Single Project View)
- `/contact` (Contact Form & Map)

## ✍️ Coding Standards
- Write clean, type-safe TypeScript code.
- Always use `'use client'` explicitly on interactive components (Language Switcher, Theme Switcher, Lightbox, Mobile Nav Drawer).
- Do not leave unfinished TODO comments or omitted code blocks.